,"closed_at":"2025-12-17T10:30:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nI've reproduced this issue in Godot 4.5.1-stable and 4.4-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-11800H @ 2.30GHz (16 threads) - 15.78 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe TextEdit function get_caret_column() is returning the wrong position when selecting a word or line. It should return the caret position at the start of the selection, instead it's returning the position after the selection.\n\nThis happens when double or triple clicking a word or line in the TextEdit object at runtime, and when select_word_under_caret() is called. It does not happen when selecting characters manually.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project with a TextEdit object\n- Monitor output from get_caret_column()\n- Select a word or line by double or triple clicking it, or use get_word_under_caret() to select a word\n\nI have provided an MRP that demonstrates the issue. Just open it and run. The caret column position will output to the console\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[text-edit-caret-col-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24209769/text-edit-caret-col-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"panttebread","id":40289899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMjg5ODk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40289899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/panttebread","html_url":"https://github.com/panttebread","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/panttebread/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/panttebread/follow